      "id": "SC4001",
      "rule": "missing-owner",
      "kind": "uncertifiable",
      "severity": "error",
      "message": "onSettled returns a cleanup function in a scope with no owner to register it on; Solid throws SETTLED_CLEANUP_UNOWNED here in dev, and in production the cleanup is silently dropped and will never run; available runtime facts do not prove whether this callback returns a cleanup that requires owner registration; this function is exported, so solid-checker cannot prove its callers provide an owner",
      "hint": "Call onSettled where an owner is active (a component body or computation), or wrap the scope in createRoot. Inside event handlers a returned cleanup is not supported; do the teardown explicitly instead. Resolve the callback's runtime return value to a definite cleanup or definite void before treating this as a violation. If every caller runs this exported function under an owner, make that ownership visible to solid-checker, for example by calling it from a component or computation in the project.",
      "analysisContext": "owner-callers-unenumerated",
